{
  "@context": {
    "@vocab": "https://danbri.github.io/glitchcan-minigam/inklet/finkapp/apps/vocab#"
  },
  "@id": "drift",
  "@type": "App",
  "position": 13,
  "id": "drift",
  "family": "play",
  "icon": "🪐",
  "name": "Drift City",
  "surface": "stage",
  "game": "drift",
  "url": "../../drift-city/dist/city.html",
  "desc": "The city on Titan and its stories",
  "controls": "sticks",
  "args": [
    "tale"
  ],
  "capabilities": [
    "audio",
    "vars:read",
    "vars:write",
    "story:steer"
  ],
  "variables": {
    "read": [
      "want_time",
      "want_weather",
      "card",
      "ledger",
      "minutes",
      "oilcan",
      "patch",
      "reed",
      "scale",
      "setlist",
      "stone",
      "tape",
      "tenpo",
      "ticket",
      "voucher"
    ],
    "write": [
      "here",
      "hour",
      "snowing",
      "card",
      "ledger",
      "minutes",
      "oilcan",
      "patch",
      "reed",
      "scale",
      "setlist",
      "stone",
      "tape",
      "tenpo",
      "ticket",
      "voucher"
    ]
  },
  "features": [
    "autoplay"
  ],
  "opens": "storyrunner",
  "story": "/glitchcan-minigam/drift-city/foafos-entry.fink.js",
  "notes": [
    "Drift City itself: the raymarched city on Titan (WebGPU, with a WebGL fallback) and its stories. `# APP: drift tale=peraspera` opens it on that story; `args` lists the only keys a story may pass. It obeys pause and the master volume (audio), keeps its story saves as a snapshot, and at a story's end offers the way back (drift-city/src/host.js). Its own controls, so no host pad. As a WORLD (`# WORLD: drift`, the story in the runner) it reads the story's want_time and want_weather, and writes where you are, the hour and the snow back to it. The clues are the story's VARs named by its `# hotspot:` tags: read so a found one is not offered again, written when the city finds one, and then the city re-enters the reader's scene (story:steer). Autoplay: the reader taps the story, not the city, so the city's sound must start without a tap in its own frame.",
    "From the launcher it opens the story runner on the Drift hub, whose stories open the city as their world (`# WORLD: drift`): the story is foafos's, not the city's own ink client.",
    "The clues are the VARs its stories name in `# hotspot:` tags (drift-city/story/*.fink.js); they are listed in both variables.read and variables.write. A new clue in a story needs its name in both lists, or the city cannot report finding it (the broker refuses an unlisted write)."
  ]
}
